= Conclusions and Recommendations

The funding authority's first decision concerns the unit of eligibility. Even a complete
correction of the 13 northern satellite-coded blocks would leave four other North Ridge flags
and release no construction funds under the township veto. Block eligibility alone opens the
47 originally unserved blocks. If funding for the separate \$12,585.12 evidence audit is
approved, the county can pursue disputed addresses in parallel. The base portfolios assume
the audit has separate administrative funding.

Under block reform the direct/cooperative portfolio adds #value("t2_main_hh") qualifying
opportunities for #value("t2_main_cost") and reaches at least #value("coop_min") in each
township. Using shared county backhaul increases the base total to #value("ppp_hh") at
#value("ppp_cost"), with a minimum of #value("ppp_min"). A 50% floor is infeasible under
block reform alone. After all 13 northern blocks qualify on verified evidence, a 50% floor
admits 5,311 direct/cooperative or #value("override_count") partnership opportunities.
The competitive tender cannot attain that floor.

Route measurements and signed provider offers determine which portfolio to award. At the
tested three-mile increase in each hub lateral the cooperative leads by 90 opportunities.
For either plan, verify wireless reach and busy-hour capacity at the proposed sites. After
deployment, measure successful orders and work or school use alongside the construction count.
